/*!
    \page index.html
    \title KAccountAutoconfig

    KAccountAutoconfig provides a job to perform server configuration lookup for any given email.

    It is an implementation of the autoconfig RFC:
    https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-mailmaint-autoconfig-04.html

    The job performs lookup on different providers like querying the ispdb.net database and performing MX DNS lookups.

    The queried configurations are then mapped to a generic class that can be used in other applications with a
    standardised set of accessors.

    Note that contrary to what is specified in the RFC, no login test is performed on the provided email and the found
    configurations.

    \section1 Using the Module

    \include {module-use.qdocinc} {using the c++ api}

    \section2 Building with CMake

    \include {module-use.qdocinc} {building with cmake} {KF6} {AccountAutoconfig} {KF6::AccountAutoconfig}

    \section1 API Reference

    \list
        \li \l{KAccountAutoconfig C++ Classes}
    \endlist
*/
